### Refresh Token Rotation - Manual Test Script
### Use with REST Client extension in VSCode or similar HTTP client

@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000
@phone = 09123456789

### 1. Send OTP
# @name sendOtp
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/send-otp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "phone": "{{phone}}"
}

###

### 2. Verify OTP (check console for OTP in development mode)
# @name verifyOtp
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/verify-otp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "token": "{{sendOtp.response.body.token}}",
  "otp": "123456"
}

###

@accessToken = {{verifyOtp.response.body.accessToken}}
@refreshToken = {{verifyOtp.response.body.refreshToken}}

### 3. Use Access Token (should work)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/sessions
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###

### 4. Refresh Token (Token Rotation Test)
# @name refresh1
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}"
}

###

@newAccessToken = {{refresh1.response.body.accessToken}}
@newRefreshToken = {{refresh1.response.body.refreshToken}}

### 5. Use Old Refresh Token (should fail - token reuse detection)
# This should return error: "تشخیص استفاده مجدد از توکن"
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}"
}

###

### 6. Use New Refresh Token (should work)
# @name refresh2
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{newRefreshToken}}"
}

###

### 7. View Active Sessions
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/sessions
Authorization: Bearer {{refresh2.response.body.accessToken}}

###

### 8. Logout from Current Device
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{refresh2.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{refresh2.response.body.refreshToken}}"
}

###

### 9. Try to use revoked token (should fail)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{refresh2.response.body.refreshToken}}"
}

###

### 10. Login again and test logout-all
# @name verifyOtp2
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/verify-otp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "token": "{{sendOtp.response.body.token}}",
  "otp": "123456"
}

###

### 11. Create multiple sessions (refresh multiple times)
# @name refresh3
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{verifyOtp2.response.body.refreshToken}}"
}

###

# @name refresh4
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{refresh3.response.body.refreshToken}}"
}

###

### 12. View all active sessions
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/sessions
Authorization: Bearer {{refresh4.response.body.accessToken}}

###

### 13. Logout from ALL devices
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout-all
Authorization: Bearer {{refresh4.response.body.accessToken}}

###

### 14. Try to use any token after logout-all (should fail)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{refresh4.response.body.refreshToken}}"
}

###

### Test Results Expected:
###
### ✅ Step 1-2: Successful OTP flow
### ✅ Step 3: Access token works
### ✅ Step 4: Refresh token rotates successfully
### ❌ Step 5: Old token reuse detected, all tokens revoked
### ✅ Step 6: New token works (after generating new session)
### ✅ Step 7: Active sessions visible
### ✅ Step 8: Logout from current device
### ❌ Step 9: Revoked token rejected
### ✅ Step 10-11: Multiple refreshes create token chain
### ✅ Step 12: All sessions visible
### ✅ Step 13: All tokens revoked
### ❌ Step 14: All tokens invalid after logout-all
